# Stable /dev symlink for the teleop gamepad.
#
# Installed on the HOST only, by scripts/install-udev-host.sh (make install-udev).
# NEVER run udevadm inside the container -- see CLAUDE.md.
#
# WHY: the Pro Controller is Bluetooth, so every reconnect can land on a
# different /dev/input/eventN (observed as event10, but nothing pins it there).
#
# Driven by the in-kernel hid-nintendo driver (no joycond or any other userspace
# daemon needed). Pairing itself is a HOST job (bluetoothctl); this rule only
# names the input node that appears once the controller connects.
#
# Matching on ATTRS{name} rather than the USB-style vendor:product, because over
# Bluetooth the HID ids sit on a parent node (0005:057E:2009) that is awkward to
# match, while the name is exact and readable.
#
# The controller exposes TWO input devices with different names:
#   "Pro Controller"        -> buttons + sticks   <- this is the one we want
#   "Pro Controller (IMU)"  -> gyro/accelerometer <- deliberately NOT matched
# The == below is an exact string compare, so the IMU node never matches.
#
# KERNEL=="event*" keeps the symlink off the legacy js* node. There is no js*
# node on this host anyway (joydev does not bind to hid-nintendo here), which is
# also why the ROS2 side must use the SDL2-based `joy` package and not the older
# `joy_linux`, which reads /dev/input/jsX.
#
# NOTE ON WHAT THIS SYMLINK IS ACTUALLY FOR: `joy` has NO device_path parameter
# (only device_name / device_id), so joy_node does not consume this path. Its
# value is diagnostics (`evtest /dev/input/pro_controller`) and any future direct
# evdev reader.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Pro Controller", SYMLINK+="input/pro_controller", MODE:="0666"
